# Line endings are pinned in the repository, not left to each
# machine's git config. The Go tooling (gofmt) treats CRLF as
# unformatted, and Windows CI runners checkout with core.autocrlf=true
# by default - without this file the SAME committed tree passes
# gofmt on one machine and fails on another (R07 caught exactly that:
# the first Actions runs went red on gofmt while local gates were
# green, because the runner materialized the LF blobs as CRLF).
#
# eol=lf: files stay LF in the working tree everywhere (checkout
# normalizes to LF regardless of autocrlf), which is also what the
# Go ecosystem expects. This changes nothing about the stored blobs
# (already LF) - it pins what every future checkout sees.
*.go text eol=lf
*.mod text eol=lf
*.sum text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
